\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"orderBackend001\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order backend_plan_v1 from agent 3: Director of Backend Engineering - Comprehensive Technical Plan for HOA Website Backend & Cloud Infrastructure\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nI have successfully developed a complete backend architecture plan leveraging AWS services to meet all HOA website requirements. The solution provides secure resident authentication, document storage with role-based access, public content delivery, email functionality, and an intuitive content management system for non-technical users.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 1. ARCHITECTURE OVERVIEW\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Core Services Selection:\\\\\\\\n- **Static Hosting**: S3 + CloudFront CDN for public website\\\\\\\\n- **Authentication**: AWS Cognito (User Pool + Identity Pool)\\\\\\\\n- **Document Storage**: S3 with encryption + DynamoDB for metadata\\\\\\\\n- **API Layer**: API Gateway + Lambda functions\\\\\\\\n- **Email Service**: SES for contact forms and notifications\\\\\\\\n- **Monitoring**: CloudWatch, X-Ray, and CloudTrail\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 2. AUTHENTICATION & AUTHORIZATION (COGNITO)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### User Pool Configuration:\\\\\\\\n- **Name**: HOA_UserPool\\\\\\\\n- **Sign-in**: Email (primary), Phone (optional)\\\\\\\\n- **Password Policy**: 12+ chars, uppercase, lowercase, numbers, symbols\\\\\\\\n- **MFA**: Optional for residents, mandatory for board/admins\\\\\\\\n- **User Groups**: residents, board-members, admins\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Identity Pool:\\\\\\\\n- **Name**: HOA_IdentityPool\\\\\\\\n- **Role Mapping**: Token-based by group\\\\\\\\n  - Cognito_HOAResidentsAuth_Role\\\\\\\\n  - Cognito_HOABoardAuth_Role\\\\\\\\n  - Cognito_HOAAdminsAuth_Role\\\\\\\\n  - Cognito_HOAUnauth_Role (public access)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Lambda Triggers:\\\\\\\\n- PreSignUp: Validate resident roster\\\\\\\\n- PostConfirmation: Assign groups, welcome email\\\\\\\\n- PreTokenGeneration: Inject custom claims\\\\\\\\n- CustomMessage: Branded email templates\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 3. DATA STORAGE ARCHITECTURE\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### S3 Bucket Structure:\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\nhoa-documents-prod/\\\\\\\\n├── meeting-minutes/<YEAR>/\\\\\\\\n├── financial-reports/<YEAR>/\\\\\\\\n├── newsletters/<YEAR>/\\\\\\\\n└── resident-documents/<RESIDENT-ID>/\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nhoa-public-assets-prod/\\\\\\\\n└── (CloudFront origin for static assets)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nhoa-logs-prod/\\\\\\\\n└── (Centralized logging)\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### DynamoDB Tables:\\\\\\\\n1. **DocumentMetadata**\\\\\\\\n   - PK: documentId, SK: version\\\\\\\\n   - GSIs: ByCategory, ByUploader, ByAccessLevel\\\\\\\\n   \\\\\\\\n2. **UserProfiles**\\\\\\\\n   - PK: userId\\\\\\\\n   - GSIs: ByEmail, ByRole\\\\\\\\n   \\\\\\\\n3. **ContentManagement**\\\\\\\\n   - PK: postId, SK: publishDate\\\\\\\\n   - GSIs: ByCategory, AllByDate\\\\\\\\n   \\\\\\\\n4. **AuditLog**\\\\\\\\n   - PK: auditId, SK: eventTime\\\\\\\\n   - TTL: 365 days\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Security:\\\\\\\\n- KMS encryption at rest (separate keys for S3, DynamoDB)\\\\\\\\n- TLS 1.3 minimum for all connections\\\\\\\\n- IAM policies enforce least privilege\\\\\\\\n- S3 bucket policies deny unencrypted uploads\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 4. API LAYER DESIGN\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### API Gateway Structure:\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\nhttps://api.hoa-website.org/\\\\\\\\n├── /auth (login, logout, refresh, register)\\\\\\\\n├── /documents (CRUD operations)\\\\\\\\n├── /posts (blog/news management)\\\\\\\\n├── /contact (form submission)\\\\\\\\n└── /health (monitoring)\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Lambda Functions:\\\\\\\\n- **AuthServiceFn**: Handle authentication flows\\\\\\\\n- **DocumentServiceFn**: Document management (512MB)\\\\\\\\n- **CmsHandlerFn**: Blog/news CRUD operations\\\\\\\\n- **ContactValidateFn**: Process contact forms\\\\\\\\n- **SesEventsFn**: Handle email events\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Content Management for Non-Technical Users:\\\\\\\\n- Simple file upload to designated S3 bucket\\\\\\\\n- Lambda automatically processes and publishes\\\\\\\\n- No coding required for updates\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 5. EMAIL SERVICE (SES)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Verified domain for HOA\\\\\\\\n- Templates: Contact confirmation, notifications\\\\\\\\n- SQS queue for reliable processing\\\\\\\\n- Bounce/complaint handling\\\\\\\\n- Anti-spam measures with rate limiting\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 6. INFRASTRUCTURE & DEPLOYMENT\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### CloudFront CDN:\\\\\\\\n- OAC to S3 origins\\\\\\\\n- Cache behaviors optimized by content type\\\\\\\\n- Security headers via Lambda@Edge\\\\\\\\n- SSL/TLS via ACM certificate\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### CI/CD Pipeline:\\\\\\\\n- CodePipeline: Source → Build → Deploy\\\\\\\\n- Staging environment for testing\\\\\\\\n- Manual approval for production\\\\\\\\n- Automated CloudFront invalidation\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Monitoring:\\\\\\\\n- CloudWatch alarms for errors, latency\\\\\\\\n- X-Ray tracing for API calls\\\\\\\\n- Custom dashboards for key metrics\\\\\\\\n- SNS notifications for critical alerts\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 7. SCALABILITY & COST\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Performance:\\\\\\\\n- Lambda auto-scaling\\\\\\\\n- DynamoDB on-demand billing\\\\\\\\n- CloudFront global edge locations\\\\\\\\n- API Gateway rate limiting\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Estimated Monthly Costs:\\\\\\\\n- Compute (Lambda): ~$30\\\\\\\\n- Storage (S3/DynamoDB): ~$50\\\\\\\\n- API Gateway: ~$50\\\\\\\\n- CloudFront: ~$20\\\\\\\\n- Monitoring: ~$15\\\\\\\\n- **Total: ~$165/month**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 8. SECURITY & COMPLIANCE\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- All data encrypted at rest and in transit\\\\\\\\n- MFA enforcement for privileged users\\\\\\\\n- Complete audit trail in CloudWatch\\\\\\\\n- Automated security scanning\\\\\\\\n- AWS Shield Standard protection\\\\\\\\n- Regular backup with 30-day retention\\\\\\\\n- Cross-region disaster recovery\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 9. DETERMINISTIC EXECUTION PLAN (DEP) COMPONENTS\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe following resources will be created with deterministic parameters:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. **Cognito User Pool**: HOA_UserPool\\\\\\\\n2. **S3 Buckets**: hoa-documents-prod, hoa-public-assets-prod, hoa-logs-prod\\\\\\\\n3. **DynamoDB Tables**: DocumentMetadata, UserProfiles, ContentManagement, AuditLog\\\\\\\\n4. **Lambda Functions**: 8 core functions with specific memory/runtime\\\\\\\\n5. **API Gateway**: HTTP API with custom domain\\\\\\\\n6. **CloudFront Distribution**: With OAC and caching rules\\\\\\\\n7. **Route 53**: Hosted zone for domain\\\\\\\\n8. **KMS Keys**: For encryption (alias/hoa/db, alias/hoa/s3)\\\\\\\\n9. **IAM Roles**: 15+ roles with precise permissions\\\\\\\\n10. **SES Configuration**: Domain verification and templates\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 10. KEY FEATURES DELIVERED\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n✓ Public informational website\\\\\\\\n✓ Secure resident login system\\\\\\\\n✓ Role-based access to sensitive documents\\\\\\\\n✓ Easy blog/news updates without coding\\\\\\\\n✓ Contact form with email delivery\\\\\\\\n✓ Mobile-responsive design support\\\\\\\\n✓ Automated backups and monitoring\\\\\\\\n✓ Cost-effective serverless architecture\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis comprehensive plan provides a secure, scalable, and user-friendly backend infrastructure that fully addresses all HOA website requirements while maintaining AWS best practices and cost efficiency.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"orderFrontend001\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order frontend_plan_v1 from agent 2: Comprehensive UX / UI & Lightweight CMS Plan – HOA Website\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n(orderSequenceID: frontend_plan_v1)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. INFORMATION ARCHITECTURE & NAVIGATION\\\\\\\\n   A. Audience Zones\\\\\\\\n      • Public – visible without login\\\\\\\\n        – Home (mission, hero image, call-to-action to log in / register)\\\\\\\\n        – About HOA (by-laws, board roster, FAQ)\\\\\\\\n        – Amenities / Services (pool rules, clubhouse rental, trash schedule)\\\\\\\\n        – News & Updates (latest 3 public posts)\\\\\\\\n        – Contact (form, address, Google-maps embed)\\\\\\\\n      • Resident (authenticated via Cognito)\\\\\\\\n        – Dashboard (personalized greeting, quick links)\\\\\\\\n        – Meeting Minutes (PDF list w/ tags & search)\\\\\\\\n        – Financial Reports (PDF list)\\\\\\\\n        – Resident News (full blog feed inc. restricted posts)\\\\\\\\n        – Forms & Requests (ARC request, maintenance ticket etc.)\\\\\\\\n        – Profile / Account (change password, preferences)\\\\\\\\n   B. Global Navigation\\\\\\\\n      • Desktop: horizontal top-nav with drop-downs, CTA button “Resident Login”.\\\\\\\\n      • Mobile: hamburger drawer, sticky bottom bar for Dashboard when logged in.\\\\\\\\n      • Breadcrumb trail inside Resident area for deep pages.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. NON-TECHNICAL CONTENT-MANAGEMENT WORKFLOW\\\\\\\\n   Goal: allow board members to post updates w/out code editors/CMS servers.\\\\\\\\n   A. Buckets\\\\\\\\n      • s3://hoa-site-assets – read-only public (HTML/CSS/JS build)\\\\\\\\n      • s3://hoa-news-sources – private, write access via IAM-User group “BoardEditors”\\\\\\\\n      • s3://hoa-news-public – public; generated HTML/JSON for blog\\\\\\\\n   B. Authoring Flow (Markdown-in-S3)\\\\\\\\n      • Board member writes Markdown file with simple YAML front-matter:\\\\\\\\n          ---\\\\\\\\n          title: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Pool Opens May 15th\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n          date: 2024-04-01\\\\\\\\n          visibility: public | residents\\\\\\\\n          tags: [pool, summer]\\\\\\\\n          ---\\\\\\\\n          (body…)\\\\\\\\n      • Upload via AWS Console drag-and-drop OR minimal custom upload page that uses\\\\\\\\n        AWS Amplify Storage (optional) with Cognito group BoardEditors.\\\\\\\\n      • S3 Event triggers Lambda “news-compiler”:\\\\\\\\n           – Validates front-matter / rejects malformed file via email to uploader.\\\\\\\\n           – Converts MD→HTML using pandoc or markdown-it.\\\\\\\\n           – Creates SEO-friendly slug folder in s3://hoa-news-public\\\\\\\\n           – Writes JSON summary record to s3://hoa-news-public/index.json\\\\\\\\n             with subset filtered by visibility.\\\\\\\\n      • CloudFront invalidation auto-runs to surface new content <60s.\\\\\\\\n   C. Consumption in Front-End\\\\\\\\n      • Public site fetches https://news.example.com/index.json, builds list cards.\\\\\\\\n      • Clicking a post loads generated HTML page (public or, if visibility=residents,\\\\\\\\n        JS checks Cognito token & fetches with signed CloudFront URL).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. UI IMPLEMENTATION STRATEGY\\\\\\\\n   A. Technology Choice\\\\\\\\n      • React + Vite build → outputs static files (index.html, assets) → S3\\\\\\\\n      • React Router (hash-based) for SPA navigation (works on S3 static hosting).\\\\\\\\n      • State mgmt: Context API only (light needs).\\\\\\\\n   B. Styling System\\\\\\\\n      • TailwindCSS 3 + custom color palette (HOA brand) compiled at build.\\\\\\\\n      • Component library file structure: /components/Navigation, /components/Card …\\\\\\\\n      • Dark-mode via media query.\\\\\\\\n   C. Accessibility & Responsiveness\\\\\\\\n      • WCAG 2.1 AA; target Lighthouse ≥ 95 a11y score.\\\\\\\\n      • Use semantic HTML, ARIA labels on custom controls.\\\\\\\\n      • Ensure color-contrast ≥ 4.5:1, keyboard focus ring visible.\\\\\\\\n      • Mobile-first breakpoints: sm 640px, md 768, lg 1024, xl 1280.\\\\\\\\n   D. Performance\\\\\\\\n      • All static assets fingerprinted (vite hashed filenames).\\\\\\\\n      • CloudFront + gzip & brotli; max-age=31536000, immutable.\\\\\\\\n      • Images pass through Lambda@Edge for webp & responsive sizes.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. BACKEND INTEGRATION POINTS\\\\\\\\n   A. Authentication\\\\\\\\n      • Amazon Cognito User Pool (HOA_Residents) w/ Hosted UI; front-end uses\\\\\\\\n        amplify-auth or vanilla amazon-cognito-identity-js for OAuth Code Grant.\\\\\\\\n      • After login, JWT stored in memory & rotated; Refresh token 30d.\\\\\\\\n   B. Secured Data Fetch\\\\\\\\n      • API Gateway “/secure/*” endpoints, Lambda authorizer → verifies JWT.\\\\\\\\n      • For meeting minutes / financials stored in s3://hoa-docs-private, Lambda\\\\\\\\n        returns presigned CloudFront URLs valid 5 min.\\\\\\\\n   C. Contact Form\\\\\\\\n      • Public POST to API Gateway → Lambda “contact-handler” → SES send to\\\\\\\\n        board@hoa.org; returns 200 JSON to front-end.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n5. DETERMINISTIC AWS RESOURCES REQUIRED (to be built in DEP)\\\\\\\\n   • S3  bucket hoa-site-assets  (static hosting, public-read)\\\\\\\\n   • S3  bucket hoa-news-sources (private; BoardEditors write)\\\\\\\\n   • S3  bucket hoa-news-public  (public read)\\\\\\\\n   • S3  bucket hoa-docs-private (private resident docs)\\\\\\\\n   • CloudFront distro “SiteCDN” → hoa-site-assets origin\\\\\\\\n   • CloudFront distro “NewsCDN” → hoa-news-public origin\\\\\\\\n   • CloudFront distro “DocsCDN” (OAI restricted) → hoa-docs-private\\\\\\\\n   • Lambda: news-compiler, contact-handler, image-optimizer (edge), auth layers.\\\\\\\\n   • IAM roles: LambdaExecRole, BoardEditors group (S3 PutObject on news-sources).\\\\\\\\n   • Cognito User Pool HOA_Residents (+ BoardEditors group inside).\\\\\\\\n   • API Gateway REST api “hoa-api” with /secure/* + /contact routes.\\\\\\\\n   • CloudWatch Log groups for each Lambda.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n6. NEXT-STEP RECOMMENDATIONS\\\\\\\\n   • Security review: bucket policies & CORS to least-privilege.\\\\\\\\n   • Branding assets (logo, color codes) required for final theme.\\\\\\\\n   • Gather board member email list to pre-seed Cognito users.\\\\\\\\n   • Define retention / archival rules for news & documents.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nNo additional recruitment required at this stage; plan is complete and ready for DEP synthesis.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEnd of report.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T01:57:43.410Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###clarify_domain###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Both backend and frontend plans are ready, but several deterministic parameters (e.g., custom domain, e-mail sender domain, initial administrator accounts, and branding assets) must be known before we can assemble a complete, fully-deterministic Execution Plan (DEP) and move to the Execution phase.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"1. Domain name: Do you already own a domain you would like the HOA website to use (e.g., examplehoa.org), or would you like us to register a new one? If you own one, please confirm the exact domain and whether it is already managed in AWS Route 53.\\\",\\n    \\\"2. E-mail sender domain: Which e-mail/domain should outgoing messages (contact-form confirmations, welcome e-mails, etc.) come from? Typically this matches the website domain (e.g., no-reply@examplehoa.org).\\\",\\n    \\\"3. Initial administrator accounts: Please provide the e-mail addresses of board members or administrators who should receive admin access on day one (for seeding Cognito and SES notifications). A simple list of e-mail addresses is fine.\\\",\\n    \\\"4. Branding assets: Do you have a logo, color palette, or other branding guidelines we should apply to the site’s look and feel, or should we proceed with a clean default theme that can be customized later?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###clarify_domain###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T01:59:44.157Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Depa